      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the area of a triangle with vertices given as \\((0,0)\\), \\((0,5)\\), and \\((7,12)\\), we can use the formula for the area of a triangle with coordinates \\((x_1, y_1)\\), \\((x_2, y_2)\\), and \\((x_3, y_3)\\):\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| x_1(y_2 - y_3) + x_2(y_3 - y_1) + x_3(y_1 - y_2) \\right|\n\\]\n\nHowever, in this case, we can directly recognize that the triangle is a right triangle with legs of 5 units and 7 units. The area of a right triangle is given by half the product of the lengths of its legs:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 5 \\times 7 = 17.5\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this by calculating it with the given formula in Python to make sure we get the correct result.\n```python\n# Defining the vertices\nx1, y1 = 0, 0\nx2, y2 = 0, 5\nx3, y3 = 7, 12\n\n# Using the formula for the area of the triangle\narea = 0.5 * abs(x1 * (y2 - y3) + x2 * (y3 - y1) + x3 * (y1 - y2))\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n17.5\n```\nThe area of the triangle with vertices at \\((0,0)\\), \\((0,5)\\), and \\((7,12)\\) is \\(\\boxed{17.5}\\) square units.",
