      "text": "To find the area of a triangle with vertices at the points \\((0,0)\\), \\((0,5)\\), and \\((7,12)\\), we can use the formula for the area of a triangle when the base and height are known. The base and height of the triangle are the coordinates of the points on the x-axis and y-axis, respectively.\n\nIn this problem, the base of the triangle is 7 units (the x-coordinate of the third vertex, \\((7,12)\\)), and the height of the triangle is 5 units (the y-coordinate of the first vertex plus the y-coordinate of the third vertex, 5 + 12 = 17). The area of a triangle is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the values of the base and height we have:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 7 \\times 5 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 35 = 17.5\n\\]\n\nSo, the area of the triangle is 17.5 square units. However, to show the final answer as a decimal to the nearest tenth, we simply leave the result as 17.5. Let's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the base and height of the triangle\nbase = 7       # Length along the x-axis\nheight = 5     # Length along the y-axis\n\n# Calculate the area of the triangle\narea = 0.5 * base * height\n\n# Round the area to the nearest tenth\narea_rounded = round(area, 1)\nprint(area_rounded)\n```\n```output\n17.5\n```\nThe area of the triangle with vertices at \\((0,0)\\), \\((0,5)\\), and \\((7,12)\\) is \\(\\boxed{17.5}\\) square units.",
